DESCRIPTION:-------------------------------------------------------\nModule
  5Gibson Agency Case Submission - Submission Link\n-----------------------
 --------------------------------\n\n  Instructions\n--------------\n\nPle
 ase review the [Case Analysis #1 (Gibson Agency) Instructions - Team Assig
 nment] (https://canvas.illinois.edu/courses/63702/pages/case-analysis-numb
 er-1-gibson-agency-instructions-team-assignment-3) before submitting the 
 case.\n\nFor this group assignment\, only one member from each group needs
  to submit the written report. If you need to make any revisions after the
  initial submission\, you are welcome to submit the revised version. Pleas
 e note that we will only grade the most recent submission.\n\nYour submiss
 ion should include a comprehensive written report\, followed by any releva
 nt Exhibits\, Tables\, or Appendices. These components will be evaluated t
 ogether to assess the overall quality of your work.\n\nTo facilitate our r
 eview process\, please submit your Excel sheet separately. This will allow
  us to refer to it if we have any questions regarding your exhibits. Gener
 ally\, the Exhibits are clear and self-explanatory\, so we may not need to
  consult your Excel sheet. However\, having it available will ensure we ca
 n thoroughly understand and evaluate your work.\n\n  Academic Integrity a
 nd Honesty\n--------------------------------\n\nAcademic integrity and hon
 esty are essential and non-negotiable at the University of Illinois. It is
  your duty to not only understand and abide by University guidelines (read
  Article I\, Part 4: Academic Integrity of the Illinois Student Code)\, bu
 t also to promote a culture of ethical behavior within your group and clas
 s. Ignorance is not an excuse for any academic dishonesty. Violations will
  be handled via Department\, School\, and University policies.\n\n  Next 
 Steps\n------------\n\nIf there are more items to be viewed or completed i
 n this module\, you can track them below.\n\nModule Item Completion (built
  in browser\, hidden in app)
