 ">Module 6</span></span><span class="dp-header-title">Assignment 8 - <em>P
 lease read the instructions and the case first before attempting this assi
 gnment!&nbsp\;</em></span></h2>\n</header>\n<div class="dp-content-block k
 l_activities2">\n<h3 class="dp-has-icon"><i class="fas fa-street-view" sty
 le="background-color: #ffffff\; color: #ff5f05\;" aria-hidden="true"><span
  class="dp-icon-content" style="display: none\;">&nbsp\;</span></i>Case Ov
 erview</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>This assignment is designed to ensure that you
  have carefully read and understood the Jinchang Case titled: “<a class=
 "instructure_file_link instructure_scribd_file inline_disabled" title="A S
 tartup Company in Supply Chain Crisis.pdf" href="https://canvas.illinois.e
 du/courses/63702/files/21298195?wrap=1" target="_blank" data-api-endpoint=
 "https://canvas.illinois.edu/api/v1/courses/63702/files/21298195" data-api
 -returntype="File">A Startup Company in Supply Chain Crisis.pdf</a>” Ple
 ase download the paper by clicking on the "PDF" link and read Section I. T
 he Case\, i.e.\, the first nine pages of the paper.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</p>\n</l
 i>\n<li>\n<p>The assignment focuses on your comprehension of the company
 ’s background\, its products\, and the implications of recent greenhouse
  gas (GHG) regulations on its operations.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong> It
  must be completed individually.</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>This is the
  first assignment related to the startup case. In Module 8\, you will comp
 lete a second\, capstone assignment\, Case Analysis #3. By dividing the wo
 rk into two parts\, we aim to help you engage with the material early and 
 reduce end-of-semester stress.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Through this case\, yo
 u will develop essential data analytics skills and gain insight into how c
 ompanies adapt to evolving global regulations.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n
 <div class="dp-content-block kl_content_block_0">\n<h3 class="dp-has-icon"
 ><i class="fas fa-tasks" style="color: #ff5f05\;" aria-hidden="true"><span
  class="dp-icon-content" style="display: none\;">&nbsp\;</span></i> Instru
 ctions</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Except for Question 8\, most questions are conceptu
 al and do not require calculations. Before you begin\, read the case thoro
 ughly and highlight key details.</li>\n<li>Question 8 asks you to create a
  PivotTable and upload your Excel file containing the completed table. We 
 provide the spreadsheet template in this module. Before you start the quiz
 \, download the <a class="instructure_file_link instructure_scribd_file in
 line_disabled" title="Jinchang Case - Student Template_ACCY503updated.xlsx
 " href="https://canvas.illinois.edu/courses/63702/files/21296698?wrap=1" t
 arget="_blank" data-api-endpoint="https://canvas.illinois.edu/api/v1/cours
 es/63702/files/21296698" data-api-returntype="File">Jinchang Case - Studen
 t Template.xlsx</a> spreadsheet and have it open and ready. It contains bo
 th the dataset and step-by-step instructions for creating a PivotTable.</l
 i>\n<li>For those learners who are unfamiliar with how to create a PivotTa
 ble in Excel\, we provide an <a title="A Video Guide on PivotTable" href="
 https://canvas.illinois.edu/courses/63702/pages/a-video-guide-on-pivottabl
 e" data-course-type="wikiPages" data-published="true" data-api-endpoint="h
 ttps://canvas.illinois.edu/api/v1/courses/63702/pages/a-video-guide-on-piv
 ottable" data-api-returntype="Page">instructional video</a> [Canvas page] 
 in this week’s module. Please watch the video before starting the assign
 ment.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-content-block kl_custom_block_su
 b_0">\n<h3 class="dp-has-icon"><i class="fa-star fas" style="background-co
 lor: #ffffff\; color: #ff5f05\;" aria-hidden="true"><span class="dp-icon-c
 ontent" style="display: none\;">&nbsp\;</span></i> Academic Integrity and 
 Honesty</h3>\n<p class="kl_current_child_1">Academic integrity and honesty
  are essential and non-negotiable at the University of Illinois. It is you
 r duty to not only understand and abide by University guidelines (read Art
 icle I\, Part 4: Academic Integrity of the Illinois Student Code)\, but al
 so to promote a culture of ethical behavior within your group and class. I
 gnorance is not an excuse for any academic dishonesty. Violations will be 
 handled via Department\, School\, and University policies.</p>\n</div>\n<d
 iv class="dp-content-block kl_custom_block_8_sub">\n<h3 class="dp-has-icon
 "><i class="far fa-arrow-alt-circle-right" style="color: #ff5f05\; backgro
 und-color: #ffffff\;" aria-hidden="true"><span class="dp-icon-content" sty
 le="display: none\;">&nbsp\;</span></i> Next Steps</h3>\n<p><span>If there
  are more items to be viewed or completed in this module\, you can track t
 hem below</span>.</p>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-content-block kl_custom_bloc
