CLASS:PRIVATE
DESCRIPTION:------------------------------------------------------------\nG
 ies College of Business Research Participation Extra Credit\n-------------
 -----------------------------------------------\n\n  Extra Credit via Gie
 s Business Research Lab\n---------------------------------------------\n\n
 You can earn extra credit in this course by participating in online resear
 ch conducted by Gies faculty. \n\nTo learn more about research participat
 ion for extra credit\, please visit the [Gies Business Research Lab Extra
  Credit website] (https://giesgroups.illinois.edu/gbrl/home/).\n\nFor this
  course\, you may complete a maximum of one 25- to 40-minute study for a
  maximum weight of 1% toward your course total. If you are enrolled in ot
 her courses that allow research participation extra credit\, then you may 
 complete separate studies to earn credit in those courses\, as well. If yo
 u are enrolled in multiple courses that offer this extra credit\, then you
  may select which course you would like the extra credit for a given study
  to apply to. You will need to decide this prior to the last day of class.
 \n\nPlease choose the passage below that fits with the dates of the course
 . For courses that begin in August\, use the first passage and delete the 
 second\; for courses that begin in October\, use the second passage and de
 lete the first. Remember also to remove the brackets from whichever one yo
 u keep.\n\nTo earn extra credit\, you will need to participate in an avail
 able study that occurs on or before Wednesday\, May 6\, 2026.\n\nDuring th
 e second week of class\, you will receive an email from the Gies Business 
 Research Lab with instructions on how to sign up for and complete these st
 udies. Emails will come from “The Research Participation System\,” so 
 be sure to check your spam. You will also receive email notifications when
  new studies are available. Studies fill quickly and participation is not 
 guaranteed\, so you will want to sign up early. \n\nIt is important for s
 tudents to read all weekly email communications sent by the Gies Business 
 Research Lab. Students are responsible for abiding by all study deadlines\
 , attendance policies\, and data quality expectations. Failure to do so ma
 y result in a loss of credit.\n\nIf you have questions about participating
  in research studies or are having issues with study signup\, please email
  [busresearchlab@illinois.edu] (mailto:busresearchlab@illinois.edu).\n\n 
  Next Steps\n------------\n\nIf there are more items to be viewed or compl
 eted in this module\, you can track them below.\n\nModule Item Completion 
 (built in browser\, hidden in app)
