CLASS:PRIVATE
DESCRIPTION:---------------------------\nACCY 503Teammate Evaluation\n-----
 ----------------------\n\n  Purpose\n---------\n\nAs you have participate
 d in a group/team-based project in this course\, the purpose of the Teamma
 te Evaluation is to assess the extent to which each team member engaged an
 d contributed to the team-based assignments.\n\n  Task\n------\n\nThe Tea
 mmate Evaluation allows you to provide feedback on your group members’ p
 articipation and contribution in the group project. Failing to complete th
 e Teammate Evaluation by the deadline would result in a penalty of 1% dedu
 ction from your final score. \n\nYou will rate and comment on your group 
 members’ participation and contribution to the group project. You will r
 eceive an averaged rating from your teammates. Your group members will not
  see the comments that you leave. The comments will only be visible to the
  Instructional Team. For more information on how the Teammate Evaluation i
 s applied to your grade\, refer to the [Teammate Evaluation Information] 
 (https://canvas.illinois.edu/courses/63702/pages/teammate-evaluation-infor
 mation) in Module 0.\n\nYou can view more information about the Teammate 
 Evaluation here: [Team Evaluation [PDF]Links to an external site.] (https
 ://uofi.box.com/s/1dpqqbs6qmlg55q08hwz2sveplxeny55) for questions and th
 e [Teamwork Expectations [PDF]Links to an external site.] (https://uofi.b
 ox.com/s/3mqiyv2cr6y22jslvyoxlyobz8a1sj7d) for each rating category.\n\nW
 hen you begin working on this activity\, we strongly recommend using Chro
 me or Mozilla Firefox for the best experience.\n\n  Instructions\n------
 --------\n\nYou will receive an average rating (ranging from 1 to 5) from 
 your team members as everyone completes the Teammate Evaluation in Week 8.
  This average teammate evaluation rating accounts for 5% of your final gra
 de.\n\nEarning an average rating of at least 2.5 (out of 5) will indicate 
 successful contribution to your group's efforts\, and this will enable you
  to earn all of the credit you would have otherwise earned on the group as
 signment.\n\nHowever\, earning an average rating of less than 2.5 (out of 
 5) will indicate insufficient contribution to your group's efforts. Unless
  you can provide evidence that the low rating was undeserved\, you may ear
 n at most 50% of what you would have otherwise earned on the group assignm
 ent. If the team member failed to contribute their fair share\, they will 
 receive a lower grade on the group assignment based on the average rating.
  If a team member did not contribute\, they may receive a 0 on the group a
 ssignment.\n\nTo complete the Teammate Evaluation:\n\n* Click the button a
 t the bottom of the page: "Load Teammate Evaluation in a new window."\n\n*
  On the next screen\, click "Evaluate" to begin evaluating your teammates.
 \n\nRefer to [our step-by-step walkthroughLinks to an external site.] (ht
 tps://uofi.box.com/s/5v1tcc1iq15vuzrfoqpynsy6vro18u1o) for more details a
 nd information on how to confirm that your evaluation is complete. Failing
  to complete the Teammate Evaluation by the deadline would result in a a p
 enalty of 1% deduction from your final score. \n\n  Still Have Questions
 ?\n-----------------------\n\nKindly reach out to [i-support@illinois.edu]
  (mailto:i-support@illinois.edu) if you have any questions regarding the 
 Teammate Evaluation.\n\n  Next Steps\n------------\n\nIf there are more i
 tems to be viewed or completed in this module\, you can track them below.\
 n\nModule Item Completion (built in browser\, hidden in app)
