 <p>As you have participated in a group/team-based project in this course\,
  the purpose of the Teammate Evaluation is to assess the extent to which e
 ach team member engaged and contributed to the team-based assignments.</p>
 \n</div>\n<div class="dp-content-block kl_custom_block_5">\n<h3 class="dp-
 has-icon"><i class="fas fa-clipboard-list" style="color: #ff5f05\;" aria-h
 idden="true"><span class="dp-icon-content" style="display: none\;">&nbsp\;
 </span></i> Task</h3>\n<p>The Teammate Evaluation allows you to provide fe
 edback on your group members’ participation and contribution in the grou
 p project. <strong>Failing to complete the Teammate Evaluation by the dead
 line would result in a penalty of 1% deduction from your final score.&nbsp
 \;</strong></p>\n<p>You will rate and comment on your group members’ par
 ticipation and contribution to the group project. You will receive an aver
 aged rating from your teammates. Your group members will <strong>not </str
 ong>see the comments that you leave. The comments will only be visible to 
 the Instructional Team. <span>For more information on how the Teammate Eva
 luation is applied to your grade\, refer to the&nbsp\;</span><a href="http
 s://canvas.illinois.edu/courses/63702/pages/teammate-evaluation-informatio
 n" data-course-type="wikiPages" data-published="true" data-api-endpoint="h
 ttps://canvas.illinois.edu/api/v1/courses/63702/pages/teammate-evaluation-
 information" data-api-returntype="Page">Teammate Evaluation Information</a
 ><span>&nbsp\;in Module 0.</span></p>\n<p><span>You can view more informat
 ion about the Teammate Evaluation here:</span><span>&nbsp\;</span><span><a
  class="inline_disabled external" href="https://uofi.box.com/s/1dpqqbs6qml
 g55q08hwz2sveplxeny55" target="_blank">Team Evaluation [PDF]<span class="e
 xternal_link_icon" role="presentation"><span class="screenreader-only">Lin
 ks to an external site.</span></span></a>&nbsp\;for questions&nbsp\;</span
 >and the<span>&nbsp\;</span><a class="inline_disabled external" href="http
 s://uofi.box.com/s/3mqiyv2cr6y22jslvyoxlyobz8a1sj7d" target="_blank"><span
 >Teamwork Expectations [PDF]</span><span class="external_link_icon" role="
 presentation"><span class="screenreader-only">Links to an external site.</
 span></span></a><span>&nbsp\;</span>for each rating category.</p>\n<p>When
  you begin working on this activity\, we strongly recommend using<span>&nb
 sp\;</span><strong>Chrome or Mozilla Firefox</strong><span>&nbsp\;</span>f
 or the best experience.</p>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-content-block kl_custo
 m_block_4">\n<h3 class="dp-has-icon"><i class="fas fa-tasks" style="color:
  #ff5f05\;" aria-hidden="true"><span class="dp-icon-content" style="displa
 y: none\;">&nbsp\;</span></i> Instructions</h3>\n<p>You will receive an av
 erage rating (ranging from 1 to 5) from your team members as everyone comp
 letes the Teammate Evaluation in Week 8. This average teammate evaluation 
 rating accounts for 5% of your final grade.</p>\n<p>Earning an average rat
 ing of at least 2.5 (out of 5) will indicate successful contribution to yo
 ur group's efforts\, and this will enable you to earn all of the credit yo
 u would have otherwise earned on the group assignment.</p>\n<p><span style
 ="background-color: #fbeeb8\;"><strong>However\, earning an average rating
  of less than 2.5 (out of 5) will indicate insufficient contribution to yo
 ur group's efforts. Unless you can provide evidence that the low rating wa
 s undeserved\, you may earn at most 50% of what you would have otherwise e
 arned on the group assignment.</strong></span> If the team member failed t
 o contribute their fair share\, they will receive a lower grade on the gro
 up assignment based on the average rating. If a team member did not contri
 bute\, they may receive a 0 on the group assignment.</p>\n<p>To complete t
 he Teammate Evaluation:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Click the button at the bottom of t
 he page: "Load Teammate Evaluation in a new window."</li>\n<li>On the next
  screen\, click "Evaluate" to begin evaluating your teammates.</li>\n</ol>
 \n<p>Refer to<span>&nbsp\;</span><a class="inline_disabled external" href=
 "https://uofi.box.com/s/5v1tcc1iq15vuzrfoqpynsy6vro18u1o" target="_blank">
 <span>our step-by-step walkthrough</span><span class="external_link_icon" 
 role="presentation"><span class="screenreader-only">Links to an external s
 ite.</span></span></a><span>&nbsp\;</span>for more details and information
  on how to confirm that your evaluation is complete. <strong>Failing to co
 mplete the Teammate Evaluation by the deadline would result in a a penalty
  of 1% deduction from your final score.&nbsp\;</strong></p>\n</div>\n<div 
 class="dp-content-block kl_objectives2">\n<h3 class="dp-has-icon"><i class
 ="fas fa-question" style="color: #ff5f05\;" aria-hidden="true"><span class
 ="dp-icon-content" style="display: none\;">&nbsp\;</span></i> Still Have Q
 uestions?</h3>\n<p>Kindly reach out to <a href="mailto:i-support@illinois.
 edu" target="_blank">i-support@illinois.edu</a>&nbsp\;if you have any ques
 tions regarding the Teammate Evaluation.</p>\n</div>\n<div class="dp-conte
 nt-block kl_custom_block_8_sub">\n<h3 class="dp-has-icon"><i class="far fa
