DTSTART:20260711T045900Z
DTEND:20260711T045900Z
CLASS:PRIVATE
DESCRIPTION:-------------------------------------------------\nMBA 547Resea
 rch Participation Extra Credit Option\n-----------------------------------
 --------------\n\n  Instructions\n--------------\n\nYou can earn extra cr
 edit in this course by participating in online research conducted by Gies 
 faculty. \n\nTo learn more about research participation for extra credit\
 , please visit the [Gies Business Research Lab Extra Credit website] (htt
 ps://giesgroups.illinois.edu/gbrl/home).\n\nFor this course\, you may comp
 lete a maximum of one 25- to 40-minute study for a maximum weight of 1% 
 toward your course total. If you are enrolled in other courses that allow
  research participation extra credit\, then you may complete separate stud
 ies to earn credit in those courses\, as well. If you are enrolled in mult
 iple courses that offer this extra credit\, then you may select which cour
 se you would like the extra credit for a given study to apply to. You will
  need to decide this prior to the last day of class.\n\nTo earn extra cred
 it\, you will need to participate in an available study that occurs on or 
 before Friday\, July 10\, 2026.\n\nDuring the second week of class\, you 
 will receive an email from the Gies Business Research Lab with instruction
 s on how to sign up for and complete these studies. Emails will come from 
 “The Research Participation System\,” so be sure to check your spam. Y
 ou will also receive email notifications when new studies are available. S
 tudies fill quickly and participation is not guaranteed\, so you will want
  to sign up early. \n\nIt is important for students to read all weekly em
 ail communications sent by the Gies Business Research Lab. Students are re
 sponsible for abiding by all study deadlines\, attendance policies\, and d
 ata quality expectations. Failure to do so may result in a loss of credit.
 \n\nIf you have questions about participating in research studies or are h
 aving issues with study signup\, please email [busresearchlab@illinois.ed
 u] (mailto:busresearchlab@illinois.edu).\n\n  Next Steps\n------------\n\
 nIf there are more items to be viewed or completed in this module\, you ca
 n track them below.\n\nModule Item Completion (built in browser\, hidden i
 n app)
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY: Research Participation Extra Credit Assignment [mba_547_120265_260
 490]
URL;VALUE=URI:https://canvas.illinois.edu/calendar?include_contexts=course_
 69168&month=07&year=2026#assignment_1616400
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instructu
 re-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_145590000000000001/attachments/2176028
 9/mobile_app.css"><div id="dp-wrapper" class="dp-wrapper dp-flat-sections 
 variation-2">\n    <header class="dp-header dp-flat-sections variation-2 "
  style="margin-bottom: 0px\; padding-top: 40px\; padding-bottom: 10px\;">\
 n        <h2 class="dp-heading"><span class="dp-header-pre"><span class="d
 p-header-pre-1">MBA 547</span></span><span class="dp-header-title">Researc
 h Participation Extra Credit Option</span></h2>\n    </header>\n    <div c
 lass="dp-content-block kl_custom_block_4">\n        <h3 class="dp-has-icon
 "><i class="fas fa-tasks" style="color: #ff5f05\;" aria-hidden="true"><spa
 n class="dp-icon-content" style="display: none\;">&nbsp\;</span></i> Instr
 uctions</h3>\n        <p>You can earn extra credit in this course by parti
 cipating in online research conducted by Gies faculty.&nbsp\;</p>\n       
  <p>To learn more about research participation for extra credit\, please v
 isit the<span>&nbsp\;</span><a href="https://giesgroups.illinois.edu/gbrl/
 home">Gies Business Research Lab Extra Credit website</a>.</p>\n        <p
 >For this course\, you may complete a maximum of<span>&nbsp\;</span><stron
 g>one</strong><span>&nbsp\;</span>25- to 40-minute study for a maximum wei
 ght of 1% toward your course total.&nbsp\;If you are enrolled in other cou
 rses that allow research participation extra credit\, then you may complet
 e separate studies to earn credit in those courses\, as well. If you are e
 nrolled in multiple courses that offer this extra credit\, then you may se
 lect which course you would like the extra credit for a given study to app
 ly to. You will need to decide this prior to the last day of class.</p>\n 
        <p>To earn extra credit\, you will need to participate in an availa
 ble study that occurs on or before<span>&nbsp\;</span><strong>Friday\, Jul
 y 10\, 2026</strong>.</p>\n        <p>During the second week of class\, yo
 u will receive an email from the Gies Business Research Lab with instructi
 ons on how to sign up for and complete these studies. Emails will come fro
 m “The Research Participation System\,” so be sure to check your spam.
  You will also receive email notifications when new studies are available.
  Studies fill quickly and participation is not guaranteed\, so you will wa
 nt to sign up early.&nbsp\;</p>\n        <p>It is important for students t
 o read all weekly email communications sent by the Gies Business Research 
 Lab. Students are responsible for abiding by all study deadlines\, attenda
 nce policies\, and data quality expectations. Failure to do so may result 
 in a loss of credit.</p>\n        <p>If you have questions about participa
 ting in research studies or are having issues with study signup\, please e
 mail&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:busresearchlab@illinois.edu">busresearchlab@ill
 inois.edu</a>.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class="dp-content-block kl_custom
 _block_8">\n        <h3 class="dp-has-icon"><i class="far fa-arrow-alt-cir
 cle-right" style="color: #ff5f05\;" aria-hidden="true"><span class="dp-ico
 n-content" style="display: none\;">&nbsp\;</span></i> Next Steps</h3>\n   
      <p>If there are more items to be viewed or completed in this module\,
  you can track them below.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class="dp-content-blo
 ck kl_custom_block_2" style="background-color: #12284c\; color: #ffffff\; 
 padding: 5px 5px 5px\;">\n        <p class="dp-progress-placeholder dp-mod
 ule-progress-completion" style="display: none\; background-color: #ff5f05\
 ; color: #000000\;">Module Item Completion (built in browser\, hidden in a
 pp)</p>\n    </div>\n</div><script src="https://instructure-uploads.s3.ama
 zonaws.com/account_145590000000000001/attachments/9675810/dp_app.js"></scr
 ipt>
END:VEVENT
